---
presentation: slidedeck
format: desktop
title: The Crazy Ones
subtitle: Gemini voice narration demo
author: Steve Jobs
lang: en-US
themes: [dark]
text_to_speech:
  authorized: true
narrative:
  provider: gemini
  model: gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview
  voice: male
  track: combined
  pause_seconds: 3
  groups:
    - index: 1
      slide:
        - non-conformists
        - impact
        - visionaries
        - the-ones-who-do
  direction:
    profile: >-
      For Speaker 1: A warm, reflective male campaign-film narrator. Keep the
      delivery original; do not imitate any specific person's voice.
    scene: >-
      A sparse recording studio. The words accompany a black-and-white montage
      celebrating people who challenge convention.
    style: Intimate, assured, idealistic, and cinematic without sounding theatrical.
    accent: Native pronunciation for the selected language.
    pacing: Deliberate, with clean pauses between short sentences.
    notes: Let each final phrase land before the audio ends.
---
@id non-conformists
@layout cover

# Here’s to the crazy ones.

The misfits. The rebels. The troublemakers.  
The round pegs in the square holes.  
The ones who see things differently.

@narrative
  direction:
    notes: Begin as a quiet toast, then add warmth and conviction with each phrase.
  entries:
    - en-US: >-
        Here’s to the crazy ones. The misfits. The rebels. The troublemakers.
        The round pegs in the square holes. The ones who see things differently.
    - fr-FR: >-
        Hommage aux fous. Aux marginaux. Aux rebelles. Aux fauteurs de troubles.
        Aux chevilles rondes dans les trous carrés. À ceux qui voient les choses
        différemment.
    - es-ES: >-
        Esto es para los locos. Los inadaptados. Los rebeldes. Los alborotadores.
        Las clavijas redondas en los agujeros cuadrados. Los que ven las cosas de
        forma diferente.
    - de-DE: >-
        Ein Hoch auf die Verrückten. Die Außenseiter. Die Rebellen. Die Unruhestifter.
        Die runden Stifte in den eckigen Löchern. Diejenigen, die die Dinge anders sehen.
    - nl-NL: >-
        Een ode aan de dwazen. De buitenbeentjes. De rebellen. De onruststokers.
        De ronde pinnen in de vierkante gaten. Degenen die de dingen anders zien.

---
@id impact
@layout cover

# They’re not fond of rules.

And they have no respect for the status quo.

You can quote them, disagree with them, glorify or vilify them.  
About the only thing you can’t do is ignore them.

@narrative
  direction:
    pacing: Measured and conversational; pause noticeably before the final sentence.
    notes: Give “ignore them” restrained emphasis, never a shout.
  entries:
    - en-US: >-
        They’re not fond of rules. And they have no respect for the status quo.
        You can quote them, disagree with them, glorify or vilify them.
        About the only thing you can’t do is ignore them.
    - fr-FR: >-
        Ils n’aiment pas les règles. Et ils n’ont aucun respect pour le statu quo.
        Vous pouvez les citer, être en désaccord avec eux, les glorifier ou les
        dénigrer. La seule chose que vous ne pouvez pas faire, c’est les ignorer.
    - es-ES: >-
        No les gustan las reglas. Y no sienten respeto por el statu quo.
        Puedes citarlos, discrepar con ellos, glorificarlos o vilipendiarlos.
        Lo único que no puedes hacer es ignorarlos.
    - de-DE: >-
        Sie halten nicht viel von Regeln. Und sie haben keinen Respekt vor dem
        Status quo. Man kann sie zitieren, ihnen widersprechen, sie verherrlichen
        oder verteufeln. Nur eines kann man nicht: sie ignorieren.
    - nl-NL: >-
        Ze houden niet van regels. En ze hebben geen respect voor de status quo.
        Je kunt ze citeren, het met hen oneens zijn, ze verheerlijken of zwartmaken.
        Het enige wat je niet kunt doen is ze negeren.

---
@id visionaries
@layout cover

# Because they change things.

They push the human race forward.

@narrative
  direction:
    style: Clear, hopeful, and quietly expansive.
    pacing: Slow enough to give both sentences equal weight.
  entries:
    - en-US: >-
        Because they change things. They push the human race forward.
    - fr-FR: >-
        Parce qu’ils changent les choses. Ils font avancer l’humanité.
    - es-ES: >-
        Porque cambian las cosas. Hacen avanzar a la humanidad.
    - de-DE: >-
        Denn sie verändern die Dinge. Sie bringen die Menschheit voran.
    - nl-NL: >-
        Omdat zij dingen veranderen. Zij stuwen de mensheid vooruit.

---
@id the-ones-who-do
@layout cover

# We see genius.

And while some may see them as the crazy ones, we see genius.

Because the people who are crazy enough  
to think they can change the world,  
are the ones who do.

@narrative
  direction:
    style: Build from reflection to calm certainty.
    pacing: Pause after “genius,” then finish with a firm, unhurried cadence.
    notes: Land the final four words simply and confidently.
  entries:
    - en-US: >-
        And while some may see them as the crazy ones, we see genius.
        Because the people who are crazy enough
        to think they can change the world,
        are the ones who do.
    - fr-FR: >-
        Et tandis que certains les voient comme des fous, nous voyons du génie.
        Parce que ceux qui sont assez fous pour penser qu’ils peuvent changer le
        monde sont ceux qui le font.
    - es-ES: >-
        Y mientras algunos los ven como locos, nosotros vemos genios.
        Porque quienes están lo bastante locos como para pensar que pueden cambiar
        el mundo son quienes lo hacen.
    - de-DE: >-
        Und während manche in ihnen Verrückte sehen, sehen wir Genies.
        Denn diejenigen, die verrückt genug sind zu glauben, sie könnten die Welt
        verändern, sind diejenigen, die es tun.
    - nl-NL: >-
        En terwijl sommigen hen als dwazen zien, zien wij genialiteit.
        Omdat de mensen die gek genoeg zijn om te denken dat ze de wereld kunnen
        veranderen, degenen zijn die het doen.
